        <!-- SECTION 19 -->
        <section id="buying-process" class="content-section">
          <h2>19. The Step-by-Step Buying Process</h2>
          <p>
            Purchasing property in DHA Phase 6 is among the safest real estate transactions in Pakistan because DHA operates its own central land title registry, 
            eliminating fraudulent patwari records and duplicate sales. Here is the exact step-by-step transaction workflow:
          </p>
          <ol class="workflow-steps">
            <li>
              <strong>Property Selection &amp; Initial Offer:</strong> 
              Identify the plot or house, agree on total sale demand with the owner or registered DHA estate agent, and issue a formal Token / Bayana deposit agreement.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Title Verification at DHA Head Office:</strong> 
              Apply for formal Title Verification at the DHA Lahore Main Office (Sector A Phase 6). DHA verifies original allocation/allotment letter ownership, ensures no legal disputes, caveats, or court injunctions exist.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>No Demand Certificate (NDC) Application:</strong> 
              The seller applies for the NDC. DHA inspects the site, verifies water and sewerage connections, ensures no bylaws violations exist (or assesses regularization dues), and clears all outstanding maintenance and development charges.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Taxation &amp; Stamp Duty Payment:</strong> 
              Pay government taxes via official FBR challan: Advance Tax under Section 236K (Buyer) and Section 236C (Seller) based on FBR valuation tables and Active Taxpayer status, plus Punjab Stamp Duty (typically 1% e-stamp).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Transfer Execution &amp; Biometrics:</strong> 
              Both buyer and seller appear before a DHA Transfer Officer at the Phase 6 Head Office. Biometric verification (fingerprint scanning linked with NADRA) is conducted, original documents are surrendered, and final payment balance is handed over via bank pay order.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Intimation / Allotment Letter Issuance:</strong> 
              Within 7 to 10 working days, DHA issues the official Transfer/Allotment Letter in the buyer's name. The buyer takes legal possession of the property.
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p>
            For a detailed breakdown of government taxes, withholding brackets, and transfer fees, consult our 
            <a href="/verification-and-transfer/">DHA Verification and Transfer Guide</a> and calculate exact costs with our 
            <a href="/dha-phase-6-property-calculator/">DHA Phase 6 Property Calculator</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

